cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below and cite
  the UMFI paper listed under preferred-citation, which defines the quantity
  that sharedimp computes. sharedimp does not claim a new feature-importance
  method.
title: "sharedimp: shared predictive importance via fold-internal residualization (UMFI-LR) for R"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dsc-chiba-u/sharedimp-r"
url: "https://github.com/dsc-chiba-u/sharedimp-r"
abstract: >-
  A resampling-based R implementation of the linear-regression variant of
  ultra-marginal feature importance (UMFI-LR). For each anchor feature the
  other predictors are residualized on the anchor with coefficients estimated
  inside the training split only, and the out-of-sample performance of a
  learner with and without the anchor is compared split by split. Built on
  parsnip, rsample and yardstick; companion to the Python package sharedimp
  (sharedimp-py), with which it shares one specification.
keywords:
  - feature importance
  - ultra-marginal feature importance
  - UMFI
  - residualization
  - cross-validation
  - tidymodels
  - R package
authors:
